## Reading method and precision

Use the common origin, x=.5/1 ticks and y integer ticks. An ordinary full
grid cell is dx=.05 by dy=.5; axes intentionally have unequal units:
x unit10cm, y unit1cm. Do not count the short terminal margin strips as
ordinary mathematical increments.

For a, locate the given x along the axis, move vertically to the solid curve,
then horizontally to y. For b, locate the given y, move horizontally to
the solid curve, then vertically to x. These are imaginary reading paths,
not new answer-bearing lines added to the media.

The original scan has thick/skewed ink; at normal640px a full cell is about
25px. Report y to roughly one decimal and x to roughly two decimals.
The visual ranges below are author reading brackets, not statistically
calibrated error bars, grading tolerances, exact givens or answer approvals.
No logarithm/power calculator was used to produce the eight answer values.
The spec's formula was used to construct the modern curve, not passed off as
an original-image measurement. Source prose .37 -> approximately2.3 and
.82 -> approximately6.6 remain approximate examples.

